What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/MTKP0001:00/pcie_hotplug/hotplug_enabled
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Surabhi Chythanya Kumar <schythanyaku@nvidia.com>, linux-tegra@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RW) Controls PCIe cable hotplug handling for the ConnectX-7
		endpoint on Tegra254-based NVIDIA DGX Spark systems.

		Writing 1 enables hotplug handling, writing 0 disables it.
		Reading returns the current setting. The default is 0, so the
		endpoint remains available from normal boot enumeration unless
		hotplug is explicitly opted into.

		While enabled, removing the cable tears down the endpoint and
		powers it off to save power, and re-inserting the cable powers
		it back up and re-enumerates it. Userspace takes no part in the
		cable plug and unplug path.

		On a 0 -> 1 transition the driver synchronises to the current
		cable state: with no cable present it tears the endpoint down
		and powers it off, and with a cable present but nothing
		enumerated it powers the endpoint up. If the cable is present
		and the endpoint is already up, nothing changes.

		Writing 0 only stops further hotplug handling. It does not
		restore an endpoint that has already been powered down.
